           "source": "thm-central-path-barrier-gap-and-dual-certificate",
           "source_section": "Statement",
           "quote": "For the smooth convex inequality problem of [[def-barrier-central-path-and-newton-residuals]], suppose a strict feasible exact minimizer $x_t$ of the barrier objective exists, the primal value $p^*$ is finite, and the equality multiplier is included. Use the sign convention $L(x,\\lambda,\\nu)=f_0(x)+\\lambda^Tg(x)+\\nu^T(Ax-b)$, and define $q_D(\\lambda,\\nu)=\\inf_{x\\in D}L(x,\\lambda,\\nu)$ on the common open domain $D$. Then the Lagrangian dual pair generated by $\\lambda_i=-1/(t g_i(x_t))$ has value $q_D(\\lambda,\\nu)=f_0(x_t)-m/t$, so\n$$0\\le f_0(x_t)-p^*\\le m/t.$$\nFor the conic model of [[def-conic-optimization-primal-dual-models]], suppose $x_t$ is an exact barrier minimizer and $F$ is a $\\nu$-log-homogeneous barrier. Its barrier multiplier $z_t=-\\nabla F(s_t)/t$ and equality multiplier give a dual feasible pair with gap $\\nu/t$, and hence\n$$0\\le c^Tx_t-p^*\\le\\nu/t.$$\nNo primal attainment or strong-duality assumption is used; existence of the exact barrier minimizer and finiteness of $p^*$ are required.",
